course: dictionary
lesson: 11436
title: Adapter: a device or a person
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An adapter is a small device that lets a plug fit a socket it does not normally fit. Read the words around it for clues. «Ella packed a travel adapter for her trip to Spain.» Spain has different sockets, so a travel adapter must help her plug in her things there.
explain: Adapter can also mean a person who adapts something, such as a story for film. «The adapter turned the famous book into a film script.» Ask yourself: is this a thing or a person? The verb turned tells you a person did the changing.
explain: Adapter is a noun, and its plural is adapters. Adaptor is another spelling of the same word, and both are correct. «Dad bought two adapters for the laptop and the phone.» Here the adapters are objects you can hold, not people.
fact: An adapter is a noun, so it can be the name of a thing or a person.
fact: «Adapter» and «adaptor» are two spellings of the same word.
fact: «Adapter» means a small device that connects a plug to a socket it does not normally fit.
fact: «Adapter» can also mean a person who adapts something, such as a story for film.
fact: Never overload an adapter with too many plugs, because this can be unsafe.
exercise: «Ella packed a travel adapter for her trip abroad.» What is a travel adapter? | A map of the airport | *A small device that lets a plug fit a foreign socket | A kind of foreign money | A bag for carrying clothes
exercise: «The adapter turned the old novel into a film script.» What does adapter mean here? | *A person who changes a story for film | A type of book | A small plug for a socket | A cable for a laptop
exercise: Which spelling of adapter is also correct? | adopter | adaptar | *adaptor | adapture
test: «Do not overload an adapter with too many plugs.» Why is this good advice? | *Too many plugs can be unsafe | Adapters work better when they are heavy | Too many plugs make the adapter glow | Plugs get bored if they are close together
test: What is the plural of adapter? | adapter's | *adapters | adapting | adapteres
exam: «The adapter let the old lamp fit the new socket.» What is an adapter here? | A person who writes films | *A device that lets a plug fit a socket | A kind of socket with no wires | A loud noise made by a lamp
